%description:

A defect in the azimuth that places a UE in a sectorial antenna pattern,
recorded rather than fixed. It shows only when the two ends are at different
heights -- which for a base station and a UE is always.

computeAngle() is meant to be the horizontal angle, the azimuth: the vertical
angle is computed separately by computeVerticalAngle(), and the two are passed
to the antenna pattern as independent arguments, as TR 38.901 7.3 defines it.
But it takes asin(dy / d) with d the three-dimensional distance, so the height
difference enlarges the hypotenuse and pulls the result towards the x axis. A
UE due north of a 25 m mast, 50 m away at 1.5 m, comes out at about 65 degrees
instead of 90, and a sectorial antenna's attenuation is evaluated 25 degrees
off. The fix is atan2 on the horizontal components. In the shipped suite it
would move exactly one row, channelmodel/Anisotropic-36873, the only
anisotropic scenario with a height difference: the LTE ones keep every node at
z = 0, which is the one geometry in which the defect cannot show -- and so the
suite has exercised sectorial antennas almost only where they could not
reveal it.

When fixed, drop the %expected-failure line and fold the checks into
ChannelModelGeometry, which is where they belong.

%expected-failure: the azimuth mixes height into the angle

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        bsChannelModel: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s
*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 3.5GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 10
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *m = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "bsChannelModel");

const Coord mast(0, 0, 25);
c.expectNear("a UE due north of a mast is at azimuth 90, whatever the heights",
        m->computeAngle(mast, Coord(0, 50, 1.5)), 90, 1e-9);
c.expectNear("a UE at 45 degrees is at azimuth 45, whatever the heights",
        m->computeAngle(mast, Coord(50, 50, 1.5)), 45, 1e-9);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=2 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
